# Controlled LLM Development

- Work from the repository root and keep changes narrow.
- Before changing code, read `docs/repository-rules.md` and the relevant files in `docs/agent-context/`.
- Do not commit, push, amend, rebase, force-push, or change remotes unless the user explicitly asks.
- Use task branches: `task-<hub-task-id>/<short-slug>` when a Hub task exists, otherwise `fix/<short-slug>` or `chore/<short-slug>`.
- Keep one executable task per branch. Do not mix unrelated features, fixes, and cleanup.
- Use commit messages in the form `<type>: <short summary>` with types from `docs/repository-rules.md`.
- Validate with repository commands only: `uv run ruff check hub tests`, `uv run ruff format --check hub tests`, and `uv run pytest -q`.
- For API contract changes, update REST, CLI, MCP, Web, and tests in the same pass.
- Never include secrets, real `.env` files, local databases, caches, or unrelated user changes.
- Merge into `main` auto-deploys to production via `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Treat any merge to `main` as a release: land work in `develop` first, and only promote verified code to `main`. See `deploy/CD.md` and `docs/agent-deploy-runbook.md`.
